      "title": "Built-in CLIP Encoder",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "For ease of use, you can directly encode whatever positive and negative prompts through just the `VRP` Node.\n\nHowever, to demonstrate a more versatile setup for advanced users, here only a patched model output is used and CLIP encoding is done elsewhere."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "For ease of use, you can directly encode whatever positive and negative prompts through just the `VRP` Node.\n\nHowever, to demonstrate a more versatile setup for advanced users, here only a patched model output is used and CLIP encoding is done elsewhere."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        2570,
        1440
      ],
      "size": [
        420,
        280
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 12,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Combiend Prompt / Passthrough",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "These two outputs are designed for refining using other models (e.g. Illustrious / Krea 2), so you can directly feed all the prompts you need without having to concatenate them yourselves.\n\n* `combined_prompt` - Global positive prompt plus positive prompts from all regions, combined, with newlines.\n\n- `global_prompt_passthrough` - Depending on whether `Prompt Mix` is on or off, it can be the same as `combined_prompt`. or just the global positive prompt.\n\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "These two outputs are designed for refining using other models (e.g. Illustrious / Krea 2), so you can directly feed all the prompts you need without having to concatenate them yourselves.\n\n* `combined_prompt` - Global positive prompt plus positive prompts from all regions, combined, with newlines.\n\n- `global_prompt_passthrough` - Depending on whether `Prompt Mix` is on or off, it can be the same as `combined_prompt`. or just the global positive prompt.\n\n"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
